// gRPC status error (UNAUTHENTICATED / PERMISSION_DENIED as applicable). DO NOT
// return an Assertion with authenticated = false.
//
// authenticated = false is a real answer, and it means the provider ANSWERED
// and identified the caller as nobody. Reaching it because verification failed
// reports ATTACKER-SUPPLIED INPUT as a legitimate anonymous session, and
// nothing downstream questions it because it arrived with no error.
//
// ⚠️ proto3 defaults a bool to false and does not put a false field on the wire
// at all. So the rejected-reported-as-anonymous shape is exactly what a
// provider produces by returning an empty message on a path it forgot to fail.
// That is why this is stated here rather than left to the Go implementation.
//
// # There is no capability on this wire
